cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this library, please cite this repository as below, and cite the
  original authors of each classical result it builds on, named in the README
  of lean-classical-upstream.
title: >-
  lean-elementary-cellular-automata: the radius-one rule space — growth,
  columns, rays and robustness of the elementary cellular automata,
  machine-checked in Lean 4
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Palamarchuk
    given-names: Mykola
    email: lividgreen@gmail.com
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2106-5777
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: https://github.com/lividgreen/lean-elementary-cellular-automata
url: https://lividgreen.github.io/lean-elementary-cellular-automata/
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib library on the 256 elementary cellular automata read as
  hosts nobody built to carry anything: the growing world, its merge quotient
  and its memory width, and the growing width decided at every quiescent table
  — zero at every stage or unbounded, unbounded at exactly 54 of the 128 — over
  the Wolfram numeral; the columns, windows and rays of a table that settle;
  rule 90's rays from a single cell at every rational speed; robustness to two
  cells at every scale over a class of tables; and a bracket on which tables
  replicate a pattern. No sorry, no native_decide, standard axioms only, with
  each capstone's axiom footprint asserted by a build-enforced guard.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - cellular automata
  - elementary cellular automata
  - rule 90
  - symbolic dynamics
# The concept DOI is added after the first release, as in the companion
# packages: only the concept DOI, never a per-version one (decision 2026-07-28).
